From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 06:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] vc4gfx: do not name an ARM instruction in a portable
 driver

Fourth of its kind, after 0013 (usb2otg), 0025 (dma.resource) and 0027
(sdhost), and the same one-line shape:

    static inline void vc4_dsb(void) { asm volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory"); }

The failure is worth restating because it points nowhere useful. m68k gas
parses `dsb` as the MRI define-storage-bytes directive, so the error is
".space specifies non-absolute value" against line numbers in a temporary
assembly file -- numbers that move with the optimisation level and name no
source line at all.

__sync_synchronize() is the compiler's own full barrier and emits the right
instruction for the target, including none where none is needed.
---
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_dma.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_dma.c
@@ -29,7 +29,21 @@
 extern APTR KernelBase;
 APTR DMABase = NULL;
 
-static inline void vc4_dsb(void) { asm volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory"); }
+/*
+ * A full barrier, without naming an ARM instruction in a driver that is not
+ * ARM-only any more.
+ *
+ * "dsb sy" as inline assembly is not merely unportable, it fails in a way that
+ * points nowhere: m68k gas parses `dsb` as the MRI define-storage-bytes
+ * directive and reports ".space specifies non-absolute value" against line
+ * numbers in a temporary file, which move with the optimisation level. This is
+ * the fourth driver in this tree to hit it -- see patches 0013 (usb2otg), 0025
+ * (dma.resource) and 0027 (sdhost).
+ *
+ * __sync_synchronize() is the compiler's own full barrier and emits the right
+ * instruction on every target, including none at all where none is needed.
+ */
+static inline void vc4_dsb(void) { __sync_synchronize(); }
 
 /* BCM system timer ticks at 1 MHz. */
 static inline ULONG vc4_now_us(void)
